 | *`refactor_confirmed`, `refactor_workspace_ready`* | *Set true only after explicit user confirmation of the requested refactor and cleanup, and verification of the isolated prepared worktree, respectively.* |

 *Omit unknown evidence. Follow a `question` with a concise question in the selected ticket. Report input validation failures before proceeding. Record evidence for the stage choice and confirm write scope independently of the router.*
+
+
+## *Launch a role*
+
+*Run `python3 <absolute-installed-using-theseus>/scripts/codex.py` with one JSON object on stdin. The adapter starts a fresh Codex exec process with the selected model, reasoning effort and cwd. Native `spawn_agent` accepts separate context and model settings but its tool signature has no cwd argument. Pass the selected role's brief only. Read and validate the actual changes and evidence before accepting the result.*
+
+| *Input field* | *Value* |
+| --- | --- |
+| *`role`* | *`planner`, `orchestrator`, `coder_light`, `coder`, `coder_heavy`, `reviewer` or `evaluator`. Use the planner's `coder_light` or `coder` assignment. Use `coder_heavy` when the orchestrator has decided to escalate.* |
+| *`settings`* | *Effective obstagent settings using flat `theseus.<role>` keys and `model/effort` values. The selected role's setting is required.* |
+| *`cwd`* | *Absolute path to the caller-verified working directory. The directory may be outside Git.* |
+| *`task`, `context`* | *Selected task as nonempty text and relevant context as text. Supply the requirements, applicable decisions and evidence needed by this role.* |
+| *`allowed_paths`, `allowed_sections`* | *Array of writable paths and a separate object mapping note paths to arrays of writable section headings. Paths are relative to cwd. Use empty values where the role has no write permission. Apply the scope to the actual diff separately.* |
+| *`checks`, `timeout`* | *Array of mandatory check commands. Optional timeout in seconds. The default is 1800.* |
+
+*Read a JSON result containing `outcome` and a nonempty `response`. Exit 0 means the role reported success. Exit 1 means the role reported error. Exit 2 means the adapter rejected the request or the process failed to complete with a valid result. For a blocked task, the response includes the concrete blocker and any necessary question.*
